## Summary

The implementation uses a sliding window approach with a hash map to track character positions, achieving O(n) time complexity. For Unicode handling, I've explained the differences between code units, code points, and grapheme clusters, and provided a solution that properly handles complex characters including emoji with modifiers, combining marks, and flags. The tests verify that both implementations work correctly with supplementary emoji and combining marks.

